invariant: INV-16
file: p256_point.c
catches: widemul_runtime_test
reason: one field multiply of the point addition runs under
  CH_WIDEMUL_NOT_STATED whatever answer the operation was handed, so one
  product in every addition takes the other copy. The points are the
  same. bin/widemul_runtime_test requires the P-256 operations to call
  the native copies alone under the constant-time answer.

--- old
    widemul_p256_fe_mul(widemul, &t0, &a->x, &b->x);
--- new
    widemul_p256_fe_mul(CH_WIDEMUL_NOT_STATED, &t0, &a->x, &b->x);
